steps.prompt:
Practical C moves from naming parts to working on them, under instruction. In plain words, the tasks are:

take a power assembly apart safely, naming each part as it comes off;
judge each part for condition;
put it back in the right relationship;
service a hydraulic tappet;
inspect the valve train for corrosion and wear;
check a valve spring with the test equipment;
inspect the exhaust system and say how it is maintained at intervals.

All of it is done in the workshop way: the manual open, the right tools, parts laid out in order.

Your instructor chooses the engine and the order, and stays with you. The next steps give the ideas behind each task. They are not a procedure for your engine.
